Applying r1–r4, I find no critical error, but two proof/scope gaps and one editorial minor.

1. **GAP — C3’s residual-read assumptions do not entail the canonical slot read.**

   The carrier assumes only that the read is:

   > “multiplicative on the relevant ladder monomials and agrees with residue on value-zero factors.”

   It then asserts:

   > “Consequently a slot with coherent digit \(\Gamma_t\) has canonical read  
   > \(R_{i+1,\beta_t}(\text{slot }t)=w_i^{f_{i+1}-t}\Theta_i(t)\Gamma_t.\)”

   and the proof says:

   > “Multiplying by a coherent digit proves (C3-canonical-read).”

   Agreement with residue on a value-zero factor \(g\) gives \(R(g)=\operatorname{res}(g)\); it does not imply the scalar-covariance identity
   \[
   R(M_sg)=R(M_s)\operatorname{res}(g)
   \]
   when \(g=\widehat k_t/\widehat n_i(su)\) is not itself a ladder monomial. Moreover, \(\beta_t\) is merely called “the slot grade”; the required relation \(\beta_t=s\bar\kappa_i\) is not stated. Thus the displayed hypotheses justify the ladder B-unit calculation only under an unstated graded scalar-compatibility convention. The gap propagates to (C3-canonical-read), (C3-three-reads), and the A7 cancellation claim.

2. **GAP — the revised A2 consumption implication still absorbs unstated HETOW structure.**

   A2 claims:

   > “\(\text{T1 (C5-monomial-ratio) + (C5-carry)}
   > \Longrightarrow
   > \text{the three pinned HETOW displays}.\)”

   But those displays contain the local objects
   \[
   \widehat n_2(k),\ n_2(k),\ m(k),\ Q,\ \tau(k),\ s(k),\ w_2
   \]
   and require, among other facts, the first equality
   \[
   \frac{\widehat n_2(k)}{n_2(k)}
   =
   \frac{\widehat n(m(k))}{\varpi^{m(k)}}
   \]
   and the second-level relation governing \(m(k+k')\) and the carry \(w_2\). Neither follows from C5, and these local identities are not stated as hypotheses in the span pin. C5 supplies the base monomial-ratio and \(q\)-carry algebra, but does not by itself imply all three quoted HETOW displays. This violates the exact-span rule introduced by r2.

3. **MINOR — r1 leaves the carrier sentence grammatically detached.**

   R1-1 inserts the \(z_1=\eta\) paragraph immediately after
   \[
   K_1=\mathbf F_Q(\eta),
   \]
   while the original text continues afterward with:

   > “and chosen basis \(1,\eta,\ldots,\eta^{f_1-1}\).”

   In the resulting text, that phrase is no longer syntactically attached to “fix” or “with.” The intended basis datum remains recoverable, so this is editorial rather than mathematical.

VERDICT: FINDINGS | FINDINGS: 0C + 2G + 1m
